# Gate 4 whitelist — names with no production reference YET.
#
# Two rules, both enforced:
#   1. Every entry needs a reason after the '#'.
#   2. An entry deferring to future wiring must name the TASK that wires it,
#      and the gate FAILS once that task completes. The list shrinks by
#      construction; an entry that outlives its task announces itself.
#
# History: 20 entries after Phase 2b, 13 after Phase 3 — seven expired when
# T056 wired them, which is the mechanism working rather than a coincidence.

# --- wired by the US2 scheduler loop (T061) ----------------------------------
evaluate_all      # SupervisedEngine drives RuleRunner from the loop, T061
next_wakeup       # the sleep-until-due timer, T061
mark_fired        # records a served instant, T061
prune             # scheduler retention sweep, T061
maybe_reset       # fingerprint daily reset, same sweep, T061
known_rules       # enumerated by the retention sweep, T061
forget            # the sweep drops mappings whose thread 404s, T061

# --- wired by US3 coalescing (T065) ------------------------------------------
is_due            # CoalesceWindow, the window timer, T065
drain             # CoalesceWindow, flushes on close, T065

# --- wired by US4 presence-aware routing (T068) ------------------------------
observe_runs      # presence updated from run records before routing, T068

# --- ops read surfaces: not deferred, so no task -----------------------------
describe          # runtime inspection of presence (FR-023); read by operators
entries           # audit log read side; read by operators and by tests
count             # fingerprint store size; read by operators and by tests
